const report="# MO-1307 Phase 2C resumption: stopped-run report\n\n**STOPPED / ENVIRONMENT_BLOCKER / NOT_PHASE2C_COMPLETE.** No implementation commit was created. Phase 2D is not ready and has not begun.\n\nThe fixed production launch of the packaged Windows PowerShell 5.1 helper was rejected because scripts are disabled on this host. The native surface attempt reached only evaluate request 1 (READ_SET), launched no worker, wrote no summary, and published no result. A single classification diagnostic using the same executable, arguments, environment, cwd and request returned exit 1, zero stdout bytes and 432 stderr bytes in 456.9334 ms. The original failure and diagnostic remain separate evidence.\n\nThis establishes an environment blocker for the accepted unchanged launch; it does not prove that every contract-compatible launch is impossible. Freeze section 17 does not explicitly forbid a fixed process-scoped ExecutionPolicy argument. The accepted helper README specifies -NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File, and documents Bypass for engineering tests. That engineering permission was not silently promoted into the product launch. No persistent execution policy was changed. Acceptance stopped under the user's failure policy.\n\nThe original stopped 2C publication-inspection interface blocker remains immutable historical evidence. C2C and C2CB supply the corrected wire 2.0.0, nine/four-request sequence and branded publication capability. Those authorities, the Freeze, Phase 1 foundation and successful 2A/2B handoffs were read. The resumed implementation builds on C2CB without copying semantic implementations or changing the old, 2A or 2B worktrees.\n\nThe user's exact authorization, \"Authorize this exact owned-console cleanup\", resolved the earlier automatic approval rejection. The helper checks sole console membership, parent=self and the trusted conhost image through a held native handle, detaches, then terminates only that exact owned host if still active and waits for exit. No rejected termination action was executed before authorization. The initial proposal note is intentionally retained as historical evidence; console-cleanup-authorization.json records its resolved disposition. This authorization is separate from the later script-policy blocker.\n\nPreserved engineering results must not be mistaken for final-source acceptance:\n\n| Campaign | Saved result | Scope and freshness |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Native helper acceptance1 | 32/32 witnesses; 35 invocations | Actual Windows native observations, engineering process-scoped Bypass; not product-launch acceptance. |\n| Surfaces regression2 | 47/47 | 38 surface groups + 9 API bootstrap groups; framed inspection and fixed semantic worker doubles. |\n| Publication receipt-v2 | 81/81 | 57 publication groups (55 negative, 2 positive) + 24 correction groups; prior publication revision. |\n| Supplemental surfaces | 10/10 | Post-rename errors, backpressure, identity/alias rejection and decision transport; prior publication revision. |\n| Runtime policy/deadline | 35/35 | 34 runtime groups plus one actual 10-second worker timeout; two later tests unrun. |\n| Exact native product launch | FAIL | First READ_SET only; policy denial before a valid response. |\n| Package / workspace / tracked whitespace | PASS / PASS / PASS | Read-only final structural checks, not behavioral certification. |\n\nCounts overlap across campaigns and categories; no aggregate total is claimed. Actual owned filesystem publication was exercised with synthetic inspection frames, not fabricated native certification. The fixed-result worker selects committed fixture bytes by both pins; it does not verify authority or compute readiness semantics. Production integration remains explicitly fail-closed.\n\nFinal-source freshness: __FRESHNESS__\n\nThe helper snapshot differs from current source only in one authorization-status comment. Its executable statements are unchanged, but the exact byte difference is disclosed in source-freshness.json. Publication is a substantive change: saved 81/81, 47/47 and 10/10 results cannot certify the later pending-write abort polling and added checkpoints. R26/R27 publication-wait tests were added after the saved 35/35 runtime run and remain unrun.\n\nUnfinished work is preserved without weakening acceptance:\n\n- Resolve the accepted production launch on the intended trusted installation, or make a deliberate documented contract-compatible launch-policy decision. Then rerun the bounded native campaign; do not reuse engineering Bypass receipts as production acceptance.\n- Connect and validate supervisor publication waits. CLI currently directly awaits createPublication, stagePublication and finalizePublication; the new waitOperation facility is not wired there. Cancellation of a pending write is added, but indefinitely stalled non-abortable filesystem operations and rename completion accounting remain unresolved.\n- Run R26/R27 and current-source publication/correction/surface regressions. Review the static conflict between Phase 1 N24's blanket setInterval prohibition and the new bounded publication checkpoint timer; this is a read-only finding, not an executed test failure.\n- Complete actual native nine-request evaluate and four-request verify, successful quiescence/no-overlap observations, helper timeout/late completion/aggregate exhaustion, requested cancellation boundaries and remaining safe filesystem/environment witnesses.\n- Run the required 105/105 Phase 1 regression against final resumed bytes. Historical B1/C2CB receipts are not substitutes.\n- Only after every acceptance prerequisite passes, create the single requested implementation commit with C2CB as parent. No commit, push, tag or Phase 2D integration is authorized by this stopped report as completed work.\n\nThe following table accounts for all 78 requested final-report fields. \"Implemented\" describes preserved source; it is not a completion certification.\n\n".replace('__FRESHNESS__',freshSentence)
